      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, Thanks a lot for your quick review.  Let me try to explain the requirements here :\nWe have a special requirements where some of the teams working on performance and power, wants console logging on perf image.\n\n1. Debug builds works as usual with UART console enabled and it will purely based on the Kconfig - CONFIG_SERIAL_QCOM_GENI_CONSOLE_DEFAULT_ENABLED.\n2. Perf image - by default console will remain disabled and with the fastboot or cmdline flag - qcom_geni_serial.con_enabled\u003d1, they can enable it.\n\nIMO this will not harm anything - but extending the console usage for the users who are interested for perf image too. \n\nPlease let us know your thoughts and any suggestion. We wanted to get it vetted here in ACK and then post it to upstream.",
      "parentUuid": "e12f2fbd_a82f293d",
      "revId": "4c571f456085d9f1c10611a58352dc00e95e7a3d",
